---
import CalculatorLayout from '../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
import { generateFAQ, generateSoftwareApplication } from '../utils/seo';
const faqs = [
  { 
    q: 'What is a countdown timer?', 
    a: 'A countdown timer is a versatile tool that counts down from a specified time to zero. Unlike basic timers, our advanced countdown timer supports multiple use cases: event countdowns (days until birthday, wedding, vacation), exam timers (count down to test date), workout timers (HIIT intervals, rest periods), cooking timers (multiple dishes simultaneously), presentation timers (track speaking time), and pomodoro-style focus sessions. It works in your browser and continues counting even when minimized.' 
  },
  { 
    q: 'How accurate is this online countdown timer?', 
    a: 'Our countdown timer is highly accurate because it uses your device\'s system clock and JavaScript\'s precise timing functions. For short durations (minutes/hours), it\'s accurate to within milliseconds. For long-term countdowns (days/weeks/months), it calculates the exact time remaining based on your device\'s clock and updates every second. It even accounts for leap years and time zone differences. The timer continues running accurately even if you switch tabs or minimize your browser.' 
  },
  { 
    q: 'Can I set multiple countdown timers at once?', 
    a: 'Yes! Our multi-timer feature lets you run up to 5 countdown timers simultaneously. This is perfect for: cooking multiple dishes with different cooking times, managing several workout intervals, tracking multiple project deadlines, or counting down to different events. Each timer has its own label, color, and alert settings. You can start, pause, reset, or remove individual timers independently without affecting others.' 
  },
  { 
    q: 'How do I create a countdown to a specific date?', 
    a: 'Use our "Event Countdown" mode. Simply select the target date and time (e.g., "December 25, 2024 at 12:00 AM"), give it a name like "Christmas 🎄", and the timer will show exactly how many days, hours, minutes, and seconds remain. You can create countdowns for birthdays, weddings, vacations, New Year\'s Eve, product launches, exams, retirement, or any important date. The timer updates in real-time and persists even when you close your browser.' 
  },
  { 
    q: 'Does the countdown timer work when my computer is in sleep mode?', 
    a: 'The timer uses your device\'s system clock, so when your computer wakes from sleep mode, it recalculates the correct remaining time based on the actual elapsed time. This means your countdown stays accurate even if your device sleeps. For critical countdowns, we recommend keeping your device awake or using the event countdown mode which calculates time based on the target date rather than elapsed seconds.' 
  },
  { 
    q: 'Can I use this countdown timer for presentations?', 
    a: 'Absolutely! Our Presentation Mode is specifically designed for speakers and presenters. Set your total speaking time (e.g., 20 minutes) and enable warning alerts at 5 minutes and 2 minutes remaining. The fullscreen display shows a clean, large-format countdown visible from across the room. Color changes (green → yellow → red) provide visual cues as time runs low. Perfect for TED-style talks, business presentations, lectures, and wedding speeches.' 
  },
  { 
    q: 'How do I set up a HIIT workout timer?', 
    a: 'Our Interval Timer mode is perfect for HIIT workouts. Set your work interval (e.g., 30 seconds), rest interval (e.g., 15 seconds), and number of rounds (e.g., 10). The timer will automatically cycle through work and rest periods with distinct sounds and visual indicators for each. You can also create custom workout sequences like Tabata (20s work/10s rest × 8 rounds), EMOM (Every Minute on the Minute), or AMRAP (As Many Rounds As Possible) style timers.' 
  },
  { 
    q: 'Can I save my countdown timers for later?', 
    a: 'Yes! All your timers and settings are automatically saved to your browser\'s local storage. This means when you close and reopen the page, your countdowns will still be there — including event dates, interval settings, and timer labels. No account or sign-up needed. Your data stays on your device and is never sent to any server. You can also bookmark specific timer configurations by copying the URL.' 
  },
  { 
    q: 'Is there a fullscreen mode for the countdown timer?', 
    a: 'Yes! The fullscreen mode provides a distraction-free, large-format countdown display perfect for: classrooms (students can see time remaining), presentations (visible from back of room), cooking (readable from across the kitchen), workouts (glanceable during exercise), and events (display on a large monitor or TV). The display automatically adjusts font size to fill the screen, and the background changes color as time runs low.' 
  },
  { 
    q: 'What sounds and alerts are available?', 
    a: 'Our countdown timer includes multiple alert options: (1) A gentle chime when time expires, (2) Warning alerts at customizable intervals (e.g., 5 minutes, 1 minute remaining), (3) Distinct sounds for work vs rest periods in interval mode, (4) Voice announcements of remaining time (optional), (5) Vibration alerts on mobile devices. You can adjust volume, choose different sounds, or mute all alerts entirely for quiet environments.' 
  },
  { 
    q: 'How is this different from a stopwatch?', 
    a: 'A stopwatch counts UP from zero, measuring elapsed time. A countdown timer counts DOWN to zero from a preset time. Our tool provides both plus much more: Event countdowns count down to future dates, Interval timers cycle through work/rest periods, Multi-timers run several countdowns at once, and Presentation mode is optimized for public speaking. Each mode serves a different purpose — choose based on what you need to accomplish.' 
  },
  { 
    q: 'Can I use this countdown timer for exam preparation?', 
    a: 'Yes! Our countdown timer is perfect for exam prep in multiple ways: (1) Set a countdown to your exam date to stay motivated, (2) Use focus mode for 25-50 minute study sessions with breaks, (3) Practice with timed mock exams using presentation mode, (4) Track study sessions with the multi-timer feature. Students worldwide use countdown timers to create urgency, maintain focus, and track progress toward exam dates.' 
  },
];

const schemas = [
  generateSoftwareApplication({
    name: 'Countdown Timer — Advanced Online Timer for Events, Workouts & More',
    description: 'Free advanced countdown timer with multiple modes: event countdown, interval timer, presentation timer, multi-timer, and focus timer. Set countdowns for any date, workout, or task.',
    url: '/countdown-timer',
  }),
  generateFAQ(faqs),
];

const relatedCalcs = [
  { name: 'Pomodoro Timer', href: '/pomodoro-timer', icon: '🍅', desc: 'Focus & productivity timer' },
  { name: 'Age Calculator', href: '/age-calculator', icon: '🎂', desc: 'Calculate your exact age' },
  { name: 'Word Counter', href: '/word-counter', icon: '📝', desc: 'Count words & characters' },
  { name: 'Online Ruler', href: '/online-ruler', icon: '📏', desc: 'Measure on screen' },
];

const useCases = [
  { icon: '🎄', title: 'Event Countdown', desc: 'Count down to birthdays, holidays, weddings, and special events' },
  { icon: '💪', title: 'Workout Timer', desc: 'HIIT, Tabata, EMOM intervals with work/rest cycles' },
  { icon: '🎤', title: 'Presentations', desc: 'Track speaking time with visual warnings for speakers' },
  { icon: '🍳', title: 'Cooking Timer', desc: 'Multiple timers for different dishes simultaneously' },
  { icon: '📚', title: 'Exam Prep', desc: 'Count down to test date + timed study sessions' },
  { icon: '🚀', title: 'Product Launch', desc: 'Build anticipation with a live countdown to launch' },
  { icon: '🧘', title: 'Meditation', desc: 'Timed meditation sessions with gentle alerts' },
  { icon: '🎮', title: 'Gaming', desc: 'Speedrun timers, challenge countdowns' },
];

const presetTimers = [
  { label: 'New Year 2027', icon: '🎆', date: '2027-01-01T00:00:00' },
  { label: 'Christmas', icon: '🎄', date: '2026-12-25T00:00:00' },
  { label: 'Valentine\'s Day', icon: '💝', date: '2027-02-14T00:00:00' },
  { label: '5 Minute Timer', icon: '⏰', duration: 300 },
  { label: '10 Minute Timer', icon: '🔟', duration: 600 },
  { label: '30 Minute Timer', icon: '🕐', duration: 1800 },
  { label: '1 Hour Timer', icon: '⏱️', duration: 3600 },
  { label: 'Tabata (20/10×8)', icon: '💪', intervals: { work: 20, rest: 10, rounds: 8 } },
];
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="Countdown Timer — Advanced Online Timer for Events, Workouts, Presentations & More"
  description="Free advanced online countdown timer with 6 modes: event countdown, interval timer, presentation timer, multi-timer, focus timer, and simple countdown. Customizable alerts, fullscreen, works offline."
  canonical="/countdown-timer"
  schema={schemas}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'Countdown Timer', url: '/countdown-timer' }]}
  relatedCalcs={relatedCalcs}
>

  <!-- Header -->
  <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;" class="fade-up">
    <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Time Tools</div>
    <h1 class="text-display-lg" style="color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 12px;">Advanced Countdown Timer</h1>
    <p class="text-body-lg" style="color: var(--color-body); max-width: 700px;">
      The ultimate countdown timer for every purpose. Count down to events, manage workouts, time presentations, cook multiple dishes, and more — all with customizable alerts and fullscreen mode.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- MODE TABS -->
  <div class="mode-tabs-wrap fade-up stagger-1" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
    <button class="ct-mode-tab active" data-mode="simple">⏰ Simple</button>
    <button class="ct-mode-tab" data-mode="event">📅 Event</button>
    <button class="ct-mode-tab" data-mode="interval">💪 Interval</button>
    <button class="ct-mode-tab" data-mode="presentation">🎤 Present</button>
    <button class="ct-mode-tab" data-mode="multi">📋 Multi-Timer</button>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== SIMPLE COUNTDOWN ========== -->
  <div id="simple-panel" class="calc-panel fade-up stagger-1" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
    <div class="ct-two-col">
      <div>
        <label class="label" style="margin-bottom:10px;">Set Countdown Time</label>
        <div class="time-input-grid">
          <div class="time-input-group">
            <input type="number" id="simple-hours" class="input-base input-lg" placeholder="0" min="0" max="99" value="0" aria-label="Hours" />
            <span class="time-unit">Hours</span>
          </div>
          <div class="time-input-group">
            <input type="number" id="simple-minutes" class="input-base input-lg" placeholder="0" min="0" max="59" value="5" aria-label="Minutes" />
            <span class="time-unit">Minutes</span>
          </div>
          <div class="time-input-group">
            <input type="number" id="simple-seconds" class="input-base input-lg" placeholder="0" min="0" max="59" value="0" aria-label="Seconds" />
            <span class="time-unit">Seconds</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="quick-presets-row" style="margin-top:10px;">
          {[{label:'1 min',h:0,m:1,s:0},{label:'3 min',h:0,m:3,s:0},{label:'5 min',h:0,m:5,s:0},{label:'10 min',h:0,m:10,s:0},{label:'15 min',h:0,m:15,s:0},{label:'30 min',h:0,m:30,s:0},{label:'1 hour',h:1,m:0,s:0},{label:'2 hours',h:2,m:0,s:0}].map(p => (
            <button class="preset-chip" data-h={p.h} data-m={p.m} data-s={p.s}>{p.label}</button>
          ))}
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top:10px;">
          <label for="simple-label" class="label" style="font-size:12px;">Timer Label (optional)</label>
          <input type="text" id="simple-label" class="input-base" placeholder="e.g., Laundry, Coffee, Nap..." />
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="ct-display-panel">
        <div class="ct-main-display" id="simple-display">05:00</div>
        <div class="ct-label-display" id="simple-label-display"></div>
        <div class="ct-status" id="simple-status">Ready</div>
        <div class="ct-controls-row">
          <button id="simple-start-btn" class="btn-primary btn-lg-ct">▶ Start</button>
          <button id="simple-pause-btn" class="btn-secondary btn-lg-ct" style="display:none;">⏸ Pause</button>
          <button id="simple-reset-btn" class="btn-secondary btn-lg-ct">🔄 Reset</button>
        </div>
        <button id="simple-fullscreen-btn" class="btn-secondary" style="width:100%;margin-top:8px;font-size:12px;padding:8px;">🖥️ Fullscreen</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== EVENT COUNTDOWN ========== -->
  <div id="event-panel" class="calc-panel fade-up stagger-1" style="margin-bottom:24px;display:none;">
    <div class="ct-two-col">
      <div>
        <label class="label" style="margin-bottom:10px;">Event Date & Time</label>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
          <input type="date" id="event-date" class="input-base" style="flex:1;min-width:180px;" />
          <input type="time" id="event-time" class="input-base" style="flex:1;min-width:140px;" value="00:00" />
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top:10px;">
          <label for="event-label" class="label" style="font-size:12px;">Event Name</label>
          <input type="text" id="event-label" class="input-base" placeholder="e.g., 🎄 Christmas, 🎂 Birthday, ✈️ Vacation..." />
        </div>
        <div class="quick-presets-row" style="margin-top:10px;">
          {presetTimers.filter(p => p.date).map(p => (
            <button class="preset-chip event-preset" data-date={p.date} data-label={p.label}>{p.icon} {p.label}</button>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="ct-display-panel event-display-panel">
        <div class="event-countdown-grid" id="event-countdown-grid">
          <div class="event-unit"><div class="event-value" id="event-days">0</div><div class="event-label">Days</div></div>
          <div class="event-separator">:</div>
          <div class="event-unit"><div class="event-value" id="event-hours">00</div><div class="event-label">Hours</div></div>
          <div class="event-separator">:</div>
          <div class="event-unit"><div class="event-value" id="event-minutes">00</div><div class="event-label">Minutes</div></div>
          <div class="event-separator">:</div>
          <div class="event-unit"><div class="event-value" id="event-seconds">00</div><div class="event-label">Seconds</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="ct-label-display" id="event-label-display" style="margin-top:12px;"></div>
        <div class="event-progress-bar-wrap">
          <div class="event-progress-bar" id="event-progress-bar"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="ct-status" id="event-status">Set a date to begin</div>
        <button id="event-fullscreen-btn" class="btn-secondary" style="width:100%;margin-top:8px;font-size:12px;padding:8px;">🖥️ Fullscreen</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== INTERVAL TIMER ========== -->
  <div id="interval-panel" class="calc-panel fade-up stagger-1" style="margin-bottom:24px;display:none;">
    <div class="ct-two-col">
      <div>
        <label class="label" style="margin-bottom:10px;">Interval Settings</label>
        <div class="settings-row">
          <div>
            <label for="work-duration" class="label" style="font-size:12px;">Work (seconds)</label>
            <input type="number" id="work-duration" class="input-base" value="30" min="1" max="600" />
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="rest-duration" class="label" style="font-size:12px;">Rest (seconds)</label>
            <input type="number" id="rest-duration" class="input-base" value="15" min="0" max="600" />
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="num-rounds" class="label" style="font-size:12px;">Rounds</label>
            <input type="number" id="num-rounds" class="input-base" value="8" min="1" max="99" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="quick-presets-row" style="margin-top:10px;">
          {[
            {label:'Tabata', work:20, rest:10, rounds:8},
            {label:'HIIT 30/15', work:30, rest:15, rounds:10},
            {label:'EMOM', work:60, rest:0, rounds:10},
            {label:'Boxing', work:180, rest:60, rounds:12},
            {label:'Circuit', work:45, rest:15, rounds:5},
            {label:'Stretch', work:30, rest:10, rounds:6},
          ].map(p => (
            <button class="preset-chip interval-preset" data-work={p.work} data-rest={p.rest} data-rounds={p.rounds}>{p.label}</button>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="ct-display-panel">
        <div class="interval-phase" id="interval-phase">WORK</div>
        <div class="ct-main-display" id="interval-display">30</div>
        <div class="interval-info">
          <span id="interval-round-info">Round 1 of 8</span>
        </div>
        <div class="interval-progress-dots" id="interval-dots"></div>
        <div class="ct-controls-row">
          <button id="interval-start-btn" class="btn-primary btn-lg-ct">▶ Start</button>
          <button id="interval-pause-btn" class="btn-secondary btn-lg-ct" style="display:none;">⏸ Pause</button>
          <button id="interval-reset-btn" class="btn-secondary btn-lg-ct">🔄 Reset</button>
        </div>
        <button id="interval-fullscreen-btn" class="btn-secondary" style="width:100%;margin-top:8px;font-size:12px;padding:8px;">🖥️ Fullscreen</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== PRESENTATION TIMER ========== -->
  <div id="presentation-panel" class="calc-panel fade-up stagger-1" style="margin-bottom:24px;display:none;">
    <div class="ct-two-col">
      <div>
        <label class="label" style="margin-bottom:10px;">Presentation Duration</label>
        <div class="time-input-grid">
          <div class="time-input-group">
            <input type="number" id="pres-hours" class="input-base input-lg" placeholder="0" min="0" max="23" value="0" aria-label="Hours" />
            <span class="time-unit">Hours</span>
          </div>
          <div class="time-input-group">
            <input type="number" id="pres-minutes" class="input-base input-lg" placeholder="0" min="0" max="59" value="20" aria-label="Minutes" />
            <span class="time-unit">Minutes</span>
          </div>
          <div class="time-input-group">
            <input type="number" id="pres-seconds" class="input-base input-lg" placeholder="0" min="0" max="59" value="0" aria-label="Seconds" />
            <span class="time-unit">Seconds</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top:10px;">
          <label class="label" style="font-size:12px;">Warning Alerts</label>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:6px;">
            {[5, 3, 2, 1].map(m => (
              <label style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;font-size:12px;cursor:pointer;color:var(--color-body);">
                <input type="checkbox" class="pres-warning" data-minutes={m} checked={m===5||m===2} style="accent-color:var(--color-link);" />
                {m} min warning
              </label>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="quick-presets-row" style="margin-top:10px;">
          {[{label:'Lightning Talk',m:5},{label:'TED Talk',m:18},{label:'Keynote',m:45},{label:'Lecture',m:60},{label:'Pitch',m:3},{label:'Demo',m:15}].map(p => (
            <button class="preset-chip pres-time-preset" data-m={p.m}>{p.label} ({p.m}m)</button>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="ct-display-panel pres-display-panel" id="pres-display-panel">
        <div class="pres-time-remaining" id="pres-display">20:00</div>
        <div class="pres-status" id="pres-status">Ready to present</div>
        <div class="pres-progress-bar-wrap">
          <div class="pres-progress-bar" id="pres-progress-bar"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="pres-time-info">
          <span>Elapsed: <strong id="pres-elapsed">00:00</strong></span>
          <span>Remaining: <strong id="pres-remaining">20:00</strong></span>
        </div>
        <div class="ct-controls-row">
          <button id="pres-start-btn" class="btn-primary btn-lg-ct">▶ Start</button>
          <button id="pres-pause-btn" class="btn-secondary btn-lg-ct" style="display:none;">⏸ Pause</button>
          <button id="pres-reset-btn" class="btn-secondary btn-lg-ct">🔄 Reset</button>
        </div>
        <button id="pres-fullscreen-btn" class="btn-secondary" style="width:100%;margin-top:8px;font-size:12px;padding:8px;">🖥️ Fullscreen</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== MULTI-TIMER ========== -->
  <div id="multi-panel" class="calc-panel fade-up stagger-1" style="margin-bottom:24px;display:none;">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;margin-bottom:16px;">
      <h2 style="color:var(--color-ink);font-size:18px;font-weight:600;margin:0;">📋 Multiple Timers</h2>
      <button id="add-timer-btn" class="btn-primary" style="font-size:13px;">+ Add Timer</button>
    </div>
    <div id="multi-timers-container" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(280px,1fr));gap:12px;">
      <div style="padding:20px;text-align:center;color:var(--color-muted);grid-column:1/-1;">
        No timers yet. Click "+ Add Timer" to create your first timer.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- USE CASES -->
  <div class="use-cases-grid fade-up" style="margin-bottom:40px;">
    {useCases.map(uc => (
      <div class="use-case-card">
        <div class="uc-icon">{uc.icon}</div>
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:var(--color-ink);margin-bottom:4px;">{uc.title}</h3>
        <p style="font-size:12px;color:var(--color-body);line-height:1.4;">{uc.desc}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <!-- SEO Article -->
  <div class="prose-section fade-up" style="margin-top:24px;">
    <h2 class="text-display-sm" style="color:var(--color-ink);margin-bottom:20px;">The Ultimate Countdown Timer — Every Use Case Covered</h2>
    
    <p class="text-body-md" style="color:var(--color-body);line-height:28px;margin-bottom:16px;">
      Whether you're counting down to a <strong>major life event</strong>, timing a <strong>high-intensity workout</strong>, managing a <strong>business presentation</strong>, or cooking <strong>multiple dishes</strong> simultaneously, our <strong>advanced countdown timer</strong> has you covered. With 5 specialized modes, customizable alerts, fullscreen support, and local storage for persistent timers, it's the only countdown tool you'll ever need.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-body-lg-strong" style="color:var(--color-ink);margin-top:24px;margin-bottom:12px;">5 Powerful Timer Modes for Every Situation</h3>
    <div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:16px 0 24px;border:1px solid var(--color-hairline);border-radius:var(--radius-md);">
      <table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px;color:var(--color-body);text-align:left;">
        <thead>
          <tr style="background:var(--color-canvas-soft-2);border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-hairline);font-weight:600;color:var(--color-ink);">
            <th style="padding:12px 16px;">Mode</th>
            <th style="padding:12px 16px;">Best For</th>
            <th style="padding:12px 16px;">Key Features</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {[
            ['⏰ Simple Countdown', 'Cooking, naps, parking meters, quick tasks', 'Quick presets, custom labels, fullscreen'],
            ['📅 Event Countdown', 'Birthdays, holidays, weddings, deadlines', 'Days/hours/minutes/seconds, progress bar'],
            ['💪 Interval Timer', 'HIIT, Tabata, EMOM, circuit training', 'Work/rest cycles, round tracking, phase display'],
            ['🎤 Presentation Timer', 'Speeches, lectures, pitches, demos', 'Warning alerts, elapsed time, color changes'],
            ['📋 Multi-Timer', 'Multiple dishes, projects, simultaneous tasks', 'Up to 5 independent timers, individual controls'],
          ].map(([mode, best, features]) => (
            <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-hairline);">
              <td style="padding:10px 16px;font-weight:600;">{mode}</td>
              <td style="padding:10px 16px;">{best}</td>
              <td style="padding:10px 16px;color:var(--color-muted);">{features}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3 class="text-body-lg-strong" style="color:var(--color-ink);margin-top:24px;margin-bottom:12px;">Event Countdown — Build Anticipation</h3>
    <p class="text-body-md" style="color:var(--color-body);line-height:28px;margin-bottom:16px;">
      The event countdown mode shows exactly how many <strong>days, hours, minutes, and seconds</strong> remain until your important date. Use it for: counting down to <strong>Christmas, New Year's Eve, birthdays, anniversaries</strong>, counting down to <strong>wedding day, vacation departure, graduation</strong>, tracking time until <strong>product launches, sales, promotions</strong>, or building excitement for <strong>concerts, sports events, movie releases</strong>. The progress bar shows how close the event is, and the timer persists even when you close your browser.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-body-lg-strong" style="color:var(--color-ink);margin-top:24px;margin-bottom:12px;">Interval Timer — Perfect Your Workouts</h3>
    <p class="text-body-md" style="color:var(--color-body);line-height:28px;margin-bottom:16px;">
      The interval timer is a must-have for fitness enthusiasts. It automatically cycles between <strong>work and rest periods</strong> with distinct visual and audio cues. Popular presets include: <strong>Tabata</strong> (20 seconds work, 10 seconds rest, 8 rounds), <strong>HIIT 30/15</strong> (30 seconds work, 15 seconds rest, 10 rounds), <strong>EMOM</strong> (Every Minute on the Minute — 60 seconds per round), and <strong>Boxing rounds</strong> (3 minutes work, 1 minute rest, 12 rounds). The phase display clearly shows whether you're in a WORK or REST period.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-body-lg-strong" style="color:var(--color-ink);margin-top:24px;margin-bottom:12px;">Presentation Timer — Speak with Confidence</h3>
    <p class="text-body-md" style="color:var(--color-body);line-height:28px;">
      Designed for public speakers, the presentation timer features <strong>warning alerts</strong> at customizable intervals (e.g., 5 minutes and 2 minutes remaining), a <strong>color-coded display</strong> that changes from green to yellow to red as time runs low, <strong>elapsed time tracking</strong> so you know how long you've been speaking, and a <strong>fullscreen mode</strong> perfect for displaying on a confidence monitor or second screen. Popular presets include Lightning Talk (5 min), TED Talk (18 min), and Keynote (45 min).
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <div style="margin-top:48px;" class="fade-up">
    <h2 class="text-display-sm" style="color:var(--color-ink);margin-bottom:24px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-list" style="border-top:1px solid var(--color-hairline);">
      {faqs.map((faq, i) => (
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls={`ct-faq-${i}`} id={`ct-faq-btn-${i}`}>
            <span>{faq.q}</span>
            <svg class="faq-icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M8 3v10M3 8h10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            </svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer" id={`ct-faq-${i}`} role="region" aria-labelledby={`ct-faq-btn-${i}`}>{faq.a}</div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>

</CalculatorLayout>

